  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Faro (Pharaon). Banking game. Setup: Standard 52-card deck in dealing box. Soda card (first) discarded before play. Gameplay: Players bet on any of 13 ranks on layout, predicting 'Win' (second card drawn). Dealer exposes two cards per round: Loser (first), Winner (second). Outcomes: Bet on Loser card rank = House collects. Bet on Winner rank = 1:1 payout. Copper token inverts prediction to Loser. Splits (two identical ranks) = House takes 50% of all bets on that rank. Case Keeper tracks all drawn cards. Game continues until 3 cards remain (Hock). Calling the Turn: Players may bet order of final 3 cards at 4:1. House edge: ~1.4% from splits.",
    Player: 'Welcome to Faro, the game that won the West. You see 13 card ranks on the layout. Place your chips on any rank. When the dealer draws two cardsâ€”first a Loser, then a Winnerâ€”you win if your card was the Winner. But if both cards match (a split), the house takes half your bet. Use the Case Keeper to track every card drawn. That knowledge is your edge.',
    objective: "Wager on whether a specific card rank will be the next 'Winner' or 'Loser' card drawn from the dealing box.",
    gameplay: "1. **Betting Phase**: Players place chips on any card rank on the layout, indicating a bet that card will 'Win' (be drawn as the second card in a turn). 2. **The Draw**: Dealer exposes two cards from the box in sequence. 3. **Card 1 (Loser)**: The first card is the LOSER. The House collects all bets on that rank (unless 'coppering' was used). 4. **Card 2 (Winner)**: The second card is the WINNER. The House pays 1:1 on all bets on that rank. 5. **Next Turn**: Betting resumes for the next pair of cards. The game continues until the deck is exhausted.",
    keyRules: [
      '**Soda**: The first card of the entire deck (removed before play begins; not part of gameplay).',
      '**Hock**: The last card remaining in the deck (visible in the box but rarely played).',
      '**Coppering**: A player places a hexagonal copper token on their chip to bet that a card will LOSE (be drawn first). Inverts the normal bet outcome.',
      "**Splits**: If both cards in a draw are the same rank (e.g., two 4s), the House takes half of all bets on that rank (both winning and losing bets are halved). This is the House's sole edge.",
      '**Calling the Turn**: When only 3 cards remain in the deck, players may bet on the exact order they will appear. This exotic bet pays 4:1 (or sometimes 3:1 depending on house rules).',
      '**Card Exhaustion**: Once a rank has been drawn 4 times (all cards of that rank removed), no further bets on that rank are accepted.',
      '**Even Money Bets**: Standard bets pay 1:1 on wins. No juice or commission is charged on winning bets (unique advantage vs. other gambling games).',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Any number of players can bet against a single Banker. Traditionally 1-10 players.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Card ranks: Ace (low) through King (high).',
      equipment: "1. **Dealing Box**: Special box with a slot to expose card faces while preventing double-dealing. 2. **Layout**: Pasteboard or cloth with 13 card ranks (Ace through King) where players place bets. 3. **Case Keeper**: An abacus-like device with beads to track which cards have been drawn from the deck. 4. **Coppers**: Hexagonal tokens placed on bets to indicate 'losing' prediction.",
      dealing: "Dealer (the Banker) shuffles the deck and places it in the dealing box. The first card exposed (the 'Soda') is a dead card and is removed from play. Betting then begins.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Betting Phase**: Players place chips on any card rank on the layout, indicating a bet that card will 'Win' (be drawn as the second card in a turn). 2. **The Draw**: Dealer exposes two cards from the box in sequence. 3. **Card 1 (Loser)**: The first card is the LOSER. The House collects all bets on that rank (unless 'coppering' was used). 4. **Card 2 (Winner)**: The second card is the WINNER. The House pays 1:1 on all bets on that rank. 5. **Next Turn**: Betting resumes for the next pair of cards. The game continues until the deck is exhausted.",
